    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Rows waiting in each outbox",
      "description": "The two positions in the pipeline history section 7 table that hold load in MySQL with no ceiling. Every other queue in that table is bounded - by the admission semaphore, by a fixed executor queue, or by the broker - so a run that overruns capacity settles here. PUBLISHED and COMPLETED rows are deliberately not counted: they are not backlog, and counting them would tie the query cost to table size, which has no purge policy yet (pipeline history 9.4). Read alongside drain rate, never as an absolute. Published by batch-1 alone, since a table's backlog is not a per-process quantity.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 62 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "oj-prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "lineWidth": 1, "fillOpacity": 20, "showPoints": "never", "stacking": { "mode": "normal" } }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outbox, status) (contest_outbox_backlog_rows)",
          "legendFormat": "{{outbox}} {{status}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Head-of-line lag",
      "description": "How long the row at the head of each outbox has been claimable without being claimed, measured on the MySQL clock against the same column the worker claims on. This is the half a drain-rate estimate cannot see: one row stuck at the front while the rest of the backlog drains normally leaves the estimate healthy and moves this instead. Zero also means an empty outbox, so read it next to the row counts.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 6, "x": 6, "y": 62 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "oj-prometheus" },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "lineWidth": 1, "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
